35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The taster forms show people fear a whole-year commitment. The ledger shows fixed costs are high.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The bank statements show a third of renewals need chasing. The treasurer logged six hours a month chasing.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The sign-in tally shows a quarter of members do two-thirds of the work. The rota confirms this.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,Turnout dropped a third after door charges. Quiet members feel uneasy about per-event costs.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The ledger confirms fixed costs. Mid-year joiners required hand-worked calculations, which is unsustainable.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, six hours a month is too much. We need a system that minimizes chasing.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, a flat annual fee collected once is the only way to stop the chasing.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, if we charge per event, the heavy users will feel exploited by the light users.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, but if we charge a flat fee, the light users feel they are subsidizing the heavy users.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,The mid-year joiner issue is a nightmare. We need a simple entry point.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,A flat fee protects the newcomers' privacy and simplifies the treasurer's job.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It also stops the bank statement chaos. One payment, one time.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"It ignores the inequality, but it keeps the peace.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"It removes the hesitation. You pay once, you belong.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,It is the only option that doesn't require constant recalculation.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I am leaning towards the flat fee. It preserves the culture of anonymity.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I agree. The administrative burden is the killer.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I can live with it if it stops the friction.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,It solves the hesitation problem.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,It is the most stable. Let's go with that.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
